 Tax Information\nTax Collection & Distribution\nTax Rates\nTax Sale Information\nTransferring Documents\nChecklist\nFrequently Asked Questions\nQuick Reference of Property Tax Deductions\nNew Page\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments A-H\nAuditor\nAuditor's Office\nThe Office of the Auditor is a constitutional office and has several different duties, including:\nServing as a secretary to the Board of County Commissioners and the clerk to the County Council\nKeeping accounts and issuing checks for the county (the Board of Commissioners, the Council, and other officials often look to the auditor for day-to-day operational assistance, information, and advice)\nCoordinating tax collection and distribution\nServing as the county comptroller\nKeeping up-to-date information on the transfer of property\nAuditor's Office\nMelissa Gray\n(812) 358-6161\n111 S Main Street Brownstown, IN 47220\nemail\nslide 1 to 5 of 7\nRecorder's\nOffice\nBoard of\nCommissioners\nClerk's\nOffice\nAuditor's\nOffice\nPlanning &\nZoning\nAssessor\nSurveyor's Office\nShare this page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://jacksoncounty.in.gov/government/departments_a-h/auditor/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nRESOURCES\nMeetings & Agendas\nJackson County GIS\nProperty Research\nE-Recording\nProperty Fraud Alert\nWhere do I Vote?\nSheriff's Department\nRESOURCES\nVoting Information\nZoning Ordinance\nSubdivision Control Ordinanace\nBuilding Permit Requirements\nPublic Document Center\nComprehensive Plan\nHistoric County Road Maps\nDIRECTORY\nAuditor\nAssessor\nClerk\nCommunity Corrections\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning\nTreasurer\nSurveyor\n© Copyright Jackson County, Indiana ⋅ 111 S Main Street Brownstown, IN 47220 ⋅\n(812) 358-6161\nPowered by revize. the Government Website Experts. ⋅ LOGIN\nClose\nRead More\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be use